ve_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,7981,6335,702,220,17,20,3613,11,323,24240,311,3735,264,4767,11,19067,11,323,95391,13,220,758,1246,1657,5510,646,582,5157,279,9611,11,421,3842,3613,1231,3331,803,1091,825,5163,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nOur club has 25 members, and wishes to pick a president, secretary, and treasurer.  In how many ways can we choose the officers, if individual members may hold more than one office?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8d320587540823d81c7465d3a665f8035e49f59abbf4acc2bdef6ac8de370973"},"seconds":6.689497470855713,"seed":439631521252528959,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of selecting a president, secretary, and treasurer from a club of 25 members where individual members may hold more than one office, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the number of choices for each position:**\n   - For the president, there are 25 possible choices.\n   - For the secretary, there are also 25 possible choices (since the same member can hold more than one office).\n   - For the treasurer, there are again 25 possible choices.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of ways to choose the officers:**\n   - Since the choices for each position are independent of each other, we multiply the number of choices for each position together.\n   - Therefore, the total number of ways to choose the president, secretary, and treasurer is \\(25 \\times 25 \\times 25 = 25^3\\).\n\n3. **Compute \\(25^3\\):**\n   \\[\n   25^3 = 25 \\times 25 \\times 25 = 625 \\times 25 = 15625\n   \\]\n\nSo, the total number of ways to choose the president, secretary, and treasurer is \\(\\boxed{15625}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{15625}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:331"}
